<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maharaja Sayajirao University of Baroda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as MSU Baroda</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> Sayajirao University of Baroda is a public university in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vadodara">Vadodara</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, founded in 1949 and named after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayajirao-gaekwad-iii">Sayajirao Gaekwad III</a>. It grew out of Baroda College, established in 1881, and was created on the initiative of the princely family, fulfilling Sayajirao's plan for a university. It is known for its faculty of fine arts and its English-medium teaching.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maharaja-sayajirao-university-of-baroda.jpg" alt="Maharaja Sayajirao University of Baroda" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dhvani Jadav · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schematic_Map_of_The_Maharaja_Sayajirao_University_(MSU_Vadodara).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
